eyebrow: Guide · Channel partners
h1: How to run a solar channel partner programme.
lead: Partners bring volume, and they also bring disputes about who owns a lead and when commission is due. A programme with clear rules and shared visibility turns that friction into trust.
answer: Give partners their own login, define who owns a lead before they submit it, hold duplicates for review, publish commission rules, and let partners see status without calling your office.
published: 2026-10-11
sections:
  - h: Decide what a partner is
    p:
      - Dealers, agents, electricians and referrers behave differently. Write down which kinds you work with and what each is expected to do, such as refer only, survey or install.
  - h: Give partners their own space
    p:
      - A WhatsApp group puts every partner in the same room as your staff and each other. A separate login keeps each partner's leads private and keeps your internal notes internal.
  - h: Settle lead ownership early
    p:
      - Most disputes are about who found the customer first. Agree the rule in advance, then apply it the same way every time.
    list:
      - A lead belongs to the partner who submitted it first
      - A submission that matches an active enquiry is held for review
      - The partner is told the outcome and the reason
  - h: Make status visible
    p:
      - Partners ask for updates because they cannot see progress. Show them where each lead stands, using a short list of statuses.
    list:
      - Submitted
      - Under review
      - Contacted
      - Converted
      - Closed with a reason
  - h: Publish commission rules
    p:
      - State the trigger, such as advance received or installation complete, and the rate. Record each commission as pending, approved, paid or rejected, so partners can see where theirs is.
  - h: Review the programme monthly
    p:
      - Look at leads submitted, leads converted and commission outstanding per partner. Reward the ones who bring good leads and have a candid conversation with the ones who do not.
takeaways:
  - Separate login, separate view.
  - Ownership rule decided before the first lead.
  - Commission has a trigger and a visible status.
